-- title:
--   Strict LF-spaces are Hausdorff locally convex with closed steps
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a complex vector space with a topology, and let $E_0\subset E_1\subset\cdots$ be an increasing sequence of linear subspaces with $E=\bigcup_n E_n$. Assume each $E_n$, with the topology induced by $E$, is a Fréchet space, and that the topology of $E$ is the finest locally convex topology for which all inclusions $E_n\hookrightarrow E$ are continuous (a strict LF-space).
--
--   Then:
--
--   1. $E$ is a Hausdorff locally convex space;
--   2. every step $E_n$ is closed in $E$.
--
--   Local convexity holds because the finest locally convex topology with the stated continuity property is generated by the union of the seminorm families of all such topologies. Hausdorffness follows because every point lies in some Hausdorff step $E_n$ carrying the induced topology. Closedness follows because $E_n$ is complete for the induced uniform structure and $E$ is Hausdorff.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The strict inductive limit is encoded exactly as in `IsStrictLF`: the topology on $E$ equals the infimum (in Mathlib's order, i.e. the finest) of all locally convex topologies making the inclusions continuous. Nuclearity is not needed.
-- source:
--   A. M. Masullo, The Music of the Primes, frozen 20 November 2026 draft, Corollary C.1.5.13, proof, pp. 668–669. https://math216.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/the-music-of-the-primes.pdf (used implicitly: the quotient $E/F$ is a strict LF-space, hence Hausdorff locally convex with closed steps); standard, cf. Köthe, Topological Vector Spaces I, §19.

import Definitions.Def_MasulloGRH_LocallyConvex

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace MasulloGRH

theorem strictLF_hlcs_and_closed_steps (E : Type*) [AddCommGroup E] [Module ℂ E]
    [TopologicalSpace E] (X : ℕ → Submodule ℂ E) (hmono : Monotone X)
    (hexh : ∀ x : E, ∃ n, x ∈ X n) (hX : ∀ n, IsFrechet (X n))
    (htop : ‹TopologicalSpace E› =
      sInf {t | IsLocallyConvexTopology E t ∧ ∀ n, @Continuous (X n) E _ t Subtype.val}) :
    IsHLCS E ∧ ∀ n, IsClosed (X n : Set E) := by sorry

end MasulloGRH
